# folk-cwe: headless development VM (Claude Code remote environment).
# There is no physical projector here, so use the GLFW windowed
# display; the VM runs it under Xvfb with Mesa lavapipe (software
# Vulkan), which exercises the whole real render path.
Wish $::thisNode uses display "glfw" with width 1280 height 720 refreshRate -1

# There is no camera/projector pair to calibrate on this VM, so the
# builtin load-calibration program would just paint its big red
# "hasn't been calibrated" warning over everything. Suppress it and
# reproduce its uncalibrated-fallback claims (minus the warning):
Wish program "builtin-programs/calibrate/load-calibration.folk" does not run

When display /disp/ has width /displayWidth/ height /displayHeight/ {
    Claim display $disp has intrinsics [dict create \
        width $displayWidth height $displayHeight \
        fx $displayWidth fy $displayWidth \
        cx [/ $displayWidth 2.0] cy [/ $displayHeight 2.0] \
        s 0 k1 0 k2 0 p1 0 p2 0]
}
Claim the default program geometry is {tagSize 30mm top 28mm right 28mm left 157mm bottom 80mm}
